  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the scene of drinking for relief",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the scene where the man is drinking from a bottle, as the text 'when you don't have to see your ex future mother-in-law anymore' directly addresses the viewer ('you') and implies that the viewer is the person experiencing this relief. The visual of the man drinking is mapped onto the viewer's own potential experience of emotional release from a difficult interpersonal situation.",
